(Scalar Multiplication) If A is an m x n marix and k ∈ R is any scalar, then the product kA of the scalar k and the matrix A is obtained by multiplying every entry in A by k. 
That is, the ijth entry of kA is ka(sub(ij)) (where a(sub(ij)) is the ijth entry of A )

